{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":301528,"name":"William Woodruff","username":"woodruffw","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/woodruffw/{size}/37228_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-10T22:53:43.373Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003ePre-PEP thread: \u003ca href=\"https://discuss.python.org/t/pre-pep-discussion-rfc-9457-error-responses-for-package-registries/105453\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003ePre-PEP Discussion: RFC 9457 Error Responses for Package registries\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCurrent PEP text: \u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0847/\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ePEP 847 – Problem Details for the Simple Repository API | peps.python.org\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-301528-summary-of-rationale-and-motivation-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-301528-summary-of-rationale-and-motivation-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSummary of rationale and motivation\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRight now, there is no \u003cem\u003estandard\u003c/em\u003e way for package indices (i.e. services offering the Simple Repository API) to present useful error messages to users. As a result, package installers (pip, Poetry, uv) have generally converged on the lowest common denominator of rendering the HTTP status code along with its phrase.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is suboptimal because it’s (1) generic, meaning that indices with different authentication and access patterns can’t present useful errors, and (2) becoming even \u003cem\u003emore\u003c/em\u003e generic with the adoption of HTTP/2, since HTTP/2 no longer allows origins to customize the status phrase itself.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e(Generic as in “supplies very little information,” not as in “general.” It’s the opposite of general too!)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-301528-summary-of-proposed-changes-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-301528-summary-of-proposed-changes-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSummary of proposed changes\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis PEP proposes the adoption of \u003ca href=\"https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc9457/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eRFC 9457\u003c/a\u003e-style “problem details” as a uniform error representation for the Simple Repository API. The main advantages of this approach are that it’s backwards compatible (both in terms of HTTP semantics and how existing installers behave), as well as progressively enhanceable (servers can insert as little or as much context as they find useful into a standard, structured error response format).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI recommend looking at \u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0847/#appendix-1-problem-details-object-examples\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eAppendix 1\u003c/a\u003e for some (purely hypothetical) examples of how problem details can be presented by servers and rendered by clients!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs always, I look forward to the community’s feedback on this proposal \u003cimg src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/apple/slightly_smiling_face.png?v=15\" title=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCC \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/dstufft\"\u003e@dstufft\u003c/a\u003e as sponsor/delegate\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCC \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/zsol\"\u003e@zsol\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/lgonzalez\"\u003e@lgonzalez\u003c/a\u003e as co-authors\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-09-10T22:53:43.373Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":34,"reads":136,"readers_count":135,"score":407.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":108996,"topic_slug":"pep-847-problem-details-for-the-simple-repository-api","display_username":"William Woodruff","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0847/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 847 – Problem Details for the Simple Repository API | peps.python.org","clicks":22},{"url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0847/#appendix-1-problem-details-object-examples","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 847 – Problem Details for the Simple Repository API | peps.python.org","clicks":18},{"url":"https://discuss.python.org/t/pre-pep-discussion-rfc-9457-error-responses-for-package-registries/105453","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"Pre-PEP Discussion: RFC 9457 Error Responses for Package registries","clicks":9},{"url":"https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc9457/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"RFC 9457: Problem Details for HTTP APIs | RFC Editor","clicks":4}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":10}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":994,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-847-problem-details-for-the-simple-repository-api/108996/1","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":10}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":10,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":301649,"name":"Cary Hawkins","username":"cjames23","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/cjames23/{size}/32376_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-14T13:05:53.372Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI do not really have any notes on the PEP so I am just here to say thank you for it! This will be a huge quality of life improvement for me as someone who maintains a mirror being able to provide back better error messaging to users.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-09-14T13:05:53.372Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":80,"readers_count":79,"score":61.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":108996,"topic_slug":"pep-847-problem-details-for-the-simple-repository-api","display_username":"Cary Hawkins","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":3}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":66679,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-847-problem-details-for-the-simple-repository-api/108996/2","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":3}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":3,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":302371,"name":"William Woodruff","username":"woodruffw","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/woodruffw/{size}/37228_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-23T22:46:00.240Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eIt’s been almost two weeks since I opened this, so I’m just giving it a little bump/nudge to remind people to provide feedback, if they have any! I suspect this PEP isn’t very controversial but regardless \u003cimg src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/apple/slightly_smiling_face.png?v=15\" title=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":3,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-09-23T22:46:00.240Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":61,"readers_count":60,"score":17.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":108996,"topic_slug":"pep-847-problem-details-for-the-simple-repository-api","display_username":"William Woodruff","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":994,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-847-problem-details-for-the-simple-repository-api/108996/3","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":302377,"name":"Laurie O","username":"EpicWink","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/epicwink/{size}/17968_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-23T23:39:42.979Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI’m personally mostly happy with it, no blockers from me.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you want to have clients programmatically act on different problem types, you’ll need to predefine values for \u003ccode\u003etype\u003c/code\u003e (either the whole URI or just the URL path part).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe primary HTTP status I would say clients should be able to distinguish is item (package or file) not found versus invalid location (URL path).\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":4,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-09-24T23:10:46.079Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":62,"readers_count":61,"score":22.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":108996,"topic_slug":"pep-847-problem-details-for-the-simple-repository-api","display_username":"Laurie O","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":1455,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-847-problem-details-for-the-simple-repository-api/108996/4","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":302436,"name":"William Woodruff","username":"woodruffw","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/woodruffw/{size}/37228_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-24T19:19:39.582Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"EpicWink\" data-display-name=\"Laurie O\" data-post=\"4\" data-topic=\"108996\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/epicwink/48/17968_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e Laurie O:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you want to have clients programmatically act on different problem types, you’ll need to predefined values for \u003ccode\u003etype\u003c/code\u003e (either the whole URI or just the URL path part).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe had some early discussion about that, but I decided to leave it out of this PEP! I think in practice it’ll be hard to make standard programmatic suggestions here, due to the diversity in third-party indices. But the nice thing about RFC 9457 is that we can always revisit that \u003cimg src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/apple/slightly_smiling_face.png?v=15\" title=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-09-24T19:19:39.582Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":4,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":59,"readers_count":58,"score":56.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":108996,"topic_slug":"pep-847-problem-details-for-the-simple-repository-api","display_username":"William Woodruff","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":3}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":994,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-847-problem-details-for-the-simple-repository-api/108996/5","reactions":[{"id":"+1","type":"emoji","count":2},{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":3,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":302607,"name":"William Woodruff","username":"woodruffw","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/woodruffw/{size}/37228_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-28T17:42:33.127Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eIt’s been just over two weeks, so I’m hereby requesting pronouncement on this PEP from \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=